    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "We want to find the largest $4$ digit integer that can be written as $15 \\pmod{22}$.\n\nDivide $10000$ by $22$ to get $454$ with a remainder of $6$.\n\nTherefore, any number that is congruent to $15 \\pmod{22}$ must be of the form $a454$ or $a344$, where $a$ is a single digit.\n\nWe want to find the largest single digit less than $5$, so the final answer is $\\boxed{9344}$.\nThe answer is: 9344",
