    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the largest \\( 4 \\)-digit integer congruent to \\( 15 \\pmod{22} \\), we need to identify the largest \\( 4 \\)-digit number and determine if it satisfies the congruence. The largest \\( 4 \\)-digit number is 9999. We need to determine if \\( 9999 \\equiv 15 \\pmod{22} \\).\n\nFirst, we perform the division:\n\n\\[\n9999 \\div 22 = 454.4545\\ldots\n\\]\n\nSince we are interested in the remainder when subtracting multiples of 22, we actually look for the equivalent value modulo \\( 22 \\):\n\n\\[\n9999 - 9978 = 21 \\quad \\text{(since \\( 9999 = 454 \\times 22 + 21 \\))}\n\\]\n\nBut since \\( 21 < 22 \\), we need to check the incrementally next smaller number. Let's find the future place values for \\( 22 \\):\n\n\\[\n9978 \\div 22 = 453 \\quad \\text{(since \\( 9978 = 453 \\times 22 \\))}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n9999 - 9978 = 21 \\quad \\text{(direct subtraction)}\n\\]\n\nNow,\n\\[\n9999 \\equiv 21 \\pmod{22}\n\\]\n\nThe remainder is greater than 15. Thus, to decrease the remainder and hit \\( 15 \\) we must get,\n\n\\[\n9999 \\equiv 15 \\pmod{22}.\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\\[\nb - 98 \\equiv 15 \\pmod{22}.\n\\]\n\nMakes,\n\\[\n9904 \\equiv 15 \\pmod{22}.\n\\]\n\nWhich is our final answer.",
